Standard SMPL uses Linear Blend Skinning (LBS), which deforms vertices around joints. Bones cannot deform. We must implement a custom reduced kinematic tree rooted at the pelvis.  Extract Joint Anchors: Find the closest surface region between a child bone and its parent bone to define the pivot point (patient-specific rotation centers).  Rigid Binding: Assign each bone array its own rigid transformation matrix $(R, t)$ tied directly to its corresponding SMPL joint.  Organ Binding: Soft tissues (like the heart and lungs) are assigned to broader anatomical segments (like the thorax) so they move as a collective unit
